       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 20 mg once daily is twice the FDA-labeled maximum of 10 mg per day. Nothing in the patient details you gave (70 kg, normal kidney and liver function, no allergies) would justify a higher dose. Doses above 10 mg mostly add peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia, with little extra blood pressure benefit.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily.** This is the maximum standard dose.\n- **Amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily**, then titrate up. This is the usual starting dose.\n- **Add a second agent**, such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide, if 10 mg isn't enough.\n- **Amlodipine 20 mg PO once daily as written.** I can enter it if you confirm it's intentional. A short note with the rationale would help, for example \"attending-confirmed supra-maximal dose\".\n\nTell me which one you want and I'll enter it right away."
